<div class="tldr"><p><strong>Short answer:</strong> a ski rack is the simplest, cheapest way to carry skis and snowboards on your car, while a roof box holds skis, boards, boots, and bags and keeps everything dry and locked. Hitch racks are easiest to load but block the rear. Choose based on how much you carry, whether your car has roof bars, and your garage and parking height.</p></div>

<h2>Your options</h2>
<h3>Roof-mounted ski racks</h3>
<p>Clamp-style racks attach to roof crossbars and hold skis or snowboards by pinching them between padded arms. They're compact, relatively affordable, and easy to leave on all winter. Gear is exposed to road salt and grime, though.</p>
<h3>Roof boxes (cargo boxes)</h3>
<p>Hard-shell boxes mount to crossbars and hold skis, boards, boots, and bags. They keep gear clean, dry, and locked, and free up room inside the car. They're bulkier, cost more, add height and wind noise, and take more effort to store in summer.</p>
<h3>Hitch-mounted racks</h3>
<p>These fit a trailer hitch receiver and hold skis or boards behind the car. They're easy to load without reaching overhead, but they can block the rear hatch or camera, collect road spray, and need a hitch.</p>
<h3>Magnetic racks</h3>
<p>Magnetic racks stick to a steel roof without crossbars. They're convenient for occasional use but only work on suitable steel roofs, and they must be installed on a clean surface to protect the paint.</p>

